<figure class="atlas-architecture">
	<div
		class="diagram"
		role="img"
		aria-label="A reconstructed view of Atlas. Text, posed RGB frames, camera poses, and depth maps enter a shared spatial context. A transformer uses rectified flow to generate the next RGB or depth element. Generated elements return to the context, while depth can be converted to point clouds and Gaussian splats."
	>
		<div class="stage inputs">
			<p class="stage-label">Multimodal sequence</p>
			<div class="tokens">
				<span>Text</span>
				<span>Posed RGB</span>
				<span>Camera</span>
				<span>Depth</span>
			</div>
		</div>

		<span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>

		<div class="stage core documented">
			<p class="stage-label">Shared spatial context</p>
			<strong>Autoregressive transformer</strong>
			<small>Posed frames and cached activations</small>
		</div>

		<span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>

		<div class="stage generation documented">
			<p class="stage-label">Next element</p>
			<strong>Rectified-flow denoising</strong>
			<small>RGB frame or depth map</small>
		</div>

		<span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>

		<div class="stage outputs">
			<p class="stage-label">Outputs</p>
			<div class="tokens">
				<span>Image</span>
				<span>Video</span>
				<span>Depth</span>
				<span>3D</span>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="feedback inferred">
			<span aria-hidden="true">↶</span>
			<p><strong>Generated views return to context</strong><br />Selected views can act as references for later frames.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="export inferred">
			<p><strong>Geometry export</strong></p>
			<p>Depth → point cloud → completed Gaussian splat</p>
		</div>
	</div>
	<figcaption>
		A working mental model of Atlas based on public information. Solid outlines denote components described by World Labs; dashed outlines denote my interpretation of how those components may fit together.
	</figcaption>
</figure>

